From: dagu
Subject: [PATCH] native seat: do not cancel hold-repeat on another key's release

Against mutter 50.1 (Ubuntu libmutter-18). Matches mutter 51.rc
meta_seat_impl_notify_key_in_impl (GNOME #4675 / Ubuntu #2150377).

mutter 50 cleared the compositor repeat timer on any key release
or on a non-repeating press. Hold A, press B (B repeats), release
A then stopped B even though B stayed down. Folio leftover KEY_UP
made this the default path; Bluetooth/USB chords hid it.

Only the repeating key's release on the same device cancels the
timer. A non-repeating press (Ctrl) must not clear an already-
repeating key. RustDesk uinput KEY_UP of the same evdev code must
not cancel a folio hold. KEY_WAKEUP (folio GPIO46 wake line) must
not start or steal compositor hold-repeat.

---
 src/backends/native/meta-seat-impl.c | 24 +++++++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/backends/native/meta-seat-impl.c b/src/backends/native/meta-seat-impl.c
index 0000000..1111111 100644
--- a/src/backends/native/meta-seat-impl.c
+++ b/src/backends/native/meta-seat-impl.c
@@ -687,11 +687,29 @@ meta_seat_impl_notify_key_in_impl (MetaSeatImpl       *seat_impl,
       queue_event (seat_impl, state_event);
     }
 
-  if (state == 0 ||             /* key release */
-      !seat_impl->repeat ||
-      !xkb_keymap_key_repeats (xkb_state_get_keymap (seat_impl->xkb),
+  /* mutter 50 cleared the timer on any release. Hold A, press B
+   * (B repeats), release A then stopped B (GNOME #4675 / Ubuntu
+   * #2150377, fixed in 51.rc). Only the repeating key's release
+   * cancels compositor hold-repeat.
+   */
+  /* Folio GPIO46 is a wake line. KEY_WAKEUP must not steal repeat. */
+  if (key == KEY_WAKEUP)
+    return;
+
+  if (state == 0)
+    {
+      /* Another seat keyboard (RustDesk uinput) releasing the same
+       * evdev code is not a release of the folio key that started
+       * the timer.
+       */
+      if (seat_impl->repeat_key == key &&
+          (!seat_impl->repeat_device ||
+           seat_impl->repeat_device == device))
+        {
+          seat_impl->repeat_count = 0;
+          meta_seat_impl_clear_repeat_source (seat_impl);
+        }
+      else if (seat_impl->repeat_source)
+        {
+          syslog (LOG_NOTICE,
+                  "dagu folio: KEY_UP 0x%x keeps repeat key=0x%x",
+                  key, seat_impl->repeat_key);
+        }
+      return;
+    }
+
+  if (!seat_impl->repeat)
+    {
+      seat_impl->repeat_count = 0;
+      meta_seat_impl_clear_repeat_source (seat_impl);
+      return;
+    }
+
+  /* 51.rc: Ctrl / other non-repeating press must not cancel. */
+  if (!xkb_keymap_key_repeats (xkb_state_get_keymap (seat_impl->xkb),
                                keycode))
-    {
-      seat_impl->repeat_count = 0;
-      meta_seat_impl_clear_repeat_source (seat_impl);
       return;
-    }
 
   if (state == 1)               /* key press */
     seat_impl->repeat_count = 0;
